{"id": "EUVD-2026-101128", "enisaUuid": "8be285a5-9c47-3f87-aa9b-bb2305b33909", "description": "miniupnpc through 2.3.3 contains a one-byte heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the minixml parseatt function that allows malicious UPnP gateways to read past buffer bounds via crafted replies. Attackers on the local network can spoof a gateway serving device descriptions or SOAP responses ending in '=' to crash the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:32:15", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/miniupnpc-minixml-oob-read", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/blob/bf4215a7574f88aa55859db9db00e3ae58cf42d6/miniupnpc/src/minixml.c#L61", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/commit/3cfb4fb78d5ac04ed0dadc8dd842fc9e448916db", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/miniupnpc-through-2.3.3-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-minixml-parseatt"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110655", "GHSA-r8vm-xv99-82gx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f1fa15f1-22a7-3f3e-b6a8-760fcb9cdb78", "product": {"name": "miniupnpc", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e707c74f-627f-380e-9fc4-798f23de8cd1", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}], "isExploited": false}